17. Machine Learning Case Study
Definition
A machine learning case study describes how machine learning is used to solve a practical real-world problem.
It explains the problem, data collection, preprocessing, model selection, training, validation, and evaluation.
The trained model learns patterns from the data and uses them to make predictions.
A case study helps us understand the complete practical ML workflow.
18. General Steps of an ML Case Study
Step 1 — Define the Problem
Clearly identify the problem that needs to be solved.
Step 2 — Collect Data
Collect relevant data required to solve the problem.
Step 3 — Preprocess Data
Clean the data and handle missing, incorrect, or unnecessary information.
Step 4 — Select Features
Choose the important features that can help the model make predictions.
Step 5 — Split the Dataset
Divide the dataset into training, validation, and/or testing data.
Step 6 — Select the Model
Choose a suitable machine learning algorithm.
Step 7 — Train the Model
Train the selected model using the training data.
Step 8 — Validate the Model
Check the model's performance using validation data or cross-validation.
Step 9 — Test the Model
Evaluate the final model using unseen test data.
Step 10 — Evaluate Performance
Use suitable evaluation metrics to measure model performance.
Step 11 — Make Predictions
Use the trained model to make predictions on new data.
